<p>
    If you provide services such as consulting, IT development, digital marketing, legal services, or training, you must issue a
    <strong>GST-compliant service invoice</strong>.
    This guide explains the correct <strong>GST invoice format for services</strong>, required fields, SAC codes, tax calculation examples, and how to generate invoices instantly online.
</p>

<hr>

<h2>What is a GST Invoice for Services?</h2>

<p>
    A GST service invoice is a tax invoice issued by a registered service provider under the Goods and Services Tax (GST) regime in India.
    Unlike product invoices that use HSN codes, service invoices use <strong>SAC (Services Accounting Code)</strong>.
</p>

<p>The invoice must clearly mention:</p>

<ul>
    <li>Service provider name, address & GSTIN</li>
    <li>Unique invoice number & date</li>
    <li>Client details (GSTIN if registered)</li>
    <li>SAC code</li>
    <li>Description of services</li>
    <li>Taxable value</li>
    <li>CGST + SGST (Intra-state) OR IGST (Inter-state)</li>
    <li>Total invoice amount</li>
</ul>

<hr />

<div class="row">

    <div class="col">
        <h2>What is SAC Code in GST Service Invoice?</h2>

        <p>SAC stands for <strong>Services Accounting Code</strong>. It is used to classify services under GST.</p>

        <p>Examples:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>998313 – IT Consulting Services</li>
            <li>998361 – Advertising Services</li>
            <li>998314 – Software Development Services</li>
            <li>9954 – Works Contract Services</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Including the correct SAC code ensures proper tax compliance and avoids penalties.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="col">
        <h2>GST Rate for Services in India</h2>

        <p>Most services attract <strong>18% GST</strong>, but some may be taxed at 5%, 12%, or 28% depending on category.</p>

        <h3>Example GST Calculation for Services (18%)</h3>

        <p>
            Service Charges: ₹50,000<br>
            GST @@18%:
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>CGST 9% = ₹4,500</li>
            <li>SGST 9% = ₹4,500</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Total Invoice Amount = ₹59,000</strong></p>

        <p>If the client is in another state:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>IGST 18% = ₹9,000</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

</div>


